Thu Nov 26 21:00:00 UTC 2026 - Jordi Relats <4889953+jordirelats@users.noreply.github.com>

- Update to 0.5.6: removals can no longer take away more than you chose
  * 'zypper remove' also removes, without asking, every installed
    package that needs one you remove (--no-force-resolution does not
    stop it): a queue of 13 orphaned and unneeded packages took away
    341 more. Now Apply simulates the whole queue first when it
    removes packages, and applies exactly what was simulated
  * The simulation window says it simulated the whole queue (or how
    many changes cannot be simulated), shows in red the packages it
    would remove that are not in the queue, and then "Remove these
    too…" asks first; "Take the removals out of the queue" takes them
    out; "Close (the queue stays as it is)" says that closing keeps
    the queue
  * Packages, Orphaned: an orphan that something installed still needs
    cannot be ticked, and says who needs it ("orphaned" only means
    that no repository has it any more)

