- Update to 0.5.4: every button says what it acts on
  * Labels name their object: everything, the one item, the n ticked,
    or the queue ("Update everything (97)…", "Simulate only digikam",
    "Put digikam in the queue", "Apply the queue…")
  * Green only for what changes the computer now (after a question);
    buttons and answers that only fill the queue are never green and
    stand behind "To the queue:"
  * Updates: "Update everything (n)…" asks first when some rows are
    unticked, and offers to update only the ticked ones; the tray and
    the command line go through the same question
  * "Stop after this step" shows that it will stop, and the terminal
    says at once what will not run
  * No repeated labels: each Maintenance task says its own action
  * Every button has a tooltip with what it does and its command
  * The queue bar and the terminal say "the queue" / "the terminal";
    in a narrow window the queue bar's labels get short
  * Help and translations updated

