Thu Nov 26 13:00:00 UTC 2026 - Jordi Relats <4889953+jordirelats@users.noreply.github.com>

- Update to 0.5.3:
  * New Drivers page: each device with the driver it uses; proprietary
    drivers when they work better (NVIDIA, some Broadcom Wi-Fi cards),
    explained with what happens with Secure Boot; missing firmware;
    and "Not needed for this computer": firmware, microcode, drivers
    and virtual machine parts for hardware the computer does not have
  * Health check at the top of Maintenance: firmware for hardware you
    do not have, apps no longer maintained, packages from another
    vendor, weak repositories, expired keys, packages no repository
    has, apps installed twice, and what takes most room
  * Move to another computer: save the repositories (with their keys),
    the programs and the settings in a .zdesk file; opened on the other
    computer, everything goes to the queue for review
  * AppImages in Applications: open, add to the menu, look for a new
    version (keeping the old one until the new one works), protect,
    and move to the trash
  * New sections: Languages (all the languages zypper knows), Locks
    with icons, Own installers (programs installed with a .sh script),
    and Expert (every zypper command, on a form or typed)
  * Home proposes adding the computer's language to zypper when it is
    missing, so programs get their translations
  * Applications: web apps of Chromium-based browsers, and protecting
    an app so that it is never removed by mistake
  * Updates: "Refresh the repositories"; the routine editor proposes
    routines made for the computer
  * A lock on a package the queue removes runs after the removal, and
    locks keep their comment
  * Languages asked for are shown again (newer zypper says "Requested")
  * Packages: after Apply, a list such as Orphaned is shown again as it
    is now (a removed package no longer stays in it, ticked)
  * Simulate and Apply take out of the queue the removal of a package that
    is no longer installed, and say so, instead of stopping with code 104
  * Recommends squashfs and python3-solv

